{"id":"965ed512-f77e-4f61-ac0a-b8743f323606","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.028","title":"Morphoelectric diversity and specialization of primate striatal neuron types","title_zh":"灵长类纹状体神经元类型的形态电学多样性与专门化","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.028","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.028","abstract":"The basal ganglia are evolutionarily ancient subcortical nuclei that form interconnected loops with the neocortex and limbic system to regulate movement, learning, habit formation, emotion, and motivation. Their dysfunction contributes to major neurological and psychiatric disorders, yet most cellular-level insights derive from rodent studies, leaving knowledge gaps in humans and translationally relevant primate species. To address this, we generated multimodal Patch-seq data linking transcriptomic identity with morphological and electrophysiological properties in the macaque striatum-the input nucleus of the basal ganglia. We found underappreciated diversity among spiny projection neurons (SPNs), including non-canonical types, and variation aligned with functional gradients. Interneurons also exhibited spatial variation and even greater morphoelectric diversity, highlighting their functional modularity. Despite broad evolutionary conservation, we identified primate-specific features and key differences from rodent striatal neurons. By integrating molecular classification with cellular properties that shape network function, our findings provide insights into the functional organization of the primate striatum.","abstract_zh":"基底节是进化历史悠久的皮层下核团，与新皮层和边缘系统形成相互连接的环路，调节运动、学习、习惯形成、情绪和动机。其功能障碍会导致主要的神经系统和精神疾病，然而大多数细胞水平的见解源于啮齿类动物研究，在人类及具有转化相关性的灵长类物种中仍存在知识缺口。为解决这一问题，我们生成了连接转录组身份与形态学及电生理学特性的多模态Patch-seq数据，研究对象为恒猴纹状体——基底节的输入核团。我们发现棘状投影神经元（SPNs）中存在未被充分认识的多样性，包括非典型类型以及与功能梯度相一致的变异。中间神经元也呈现空间变异，并表现出更大的形态电学多样性，突显了其功能模块化。尽管存在广泛的进化保守性，我们还是发现了灵长类特异的特征以及与啮齿类纹状体神经元的关键差异。通过将分子分类与塑造网络功能的细胞特性相结合，我们的研究结果为灵长类纹状体的功能组织提供了洞察。","snippet":"The basal ganglia are evolutionarily ancient subcortical nuclei that form interconnected loops with the neocortex and limbic system to regulate movement, learning, habit formation, emotion, and motivation. Their dysfunction contributes to major neurological and psychiatric disorders, yet most cellular-level insights derive from rodent studies, leaving knowledge gaps in humans and translationally relevant primate spe…","translated_at":"2026-11-14T08:11:26.352478Z","translation_model":"nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":"189","issue":"23","published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Xiao-Ping Liu","authors_text":"Xiao-Ping Liu, Rachel Dalley, Nelson Johansen, Agata Budzillo, Julian Thijssen, Jeremy A. Miller, Sarah Walling-Bell, Scott Sawchuk, Femke Waleboer, Lauren Alfiler, Julia Andrade, Angela Ayala, Stuard Barta, Kyla Berry, Darren Bertagnolli, Ashwin Bhandiwad, Madeline Bixby, Krista Blake, Krissy Brouner, Trangthanh Cardenas, Tamara Casper, Anish Bhaswanth Chakka, Thomas Chartrand, Scott Daniel, Nicholas Donadio, Nadezhda I. Dotson, Tom Egdorf, Rachel Enstrom, Yuanyuan Fu, Amanda Gary, Jeff Goldy, Melissa Gorham, Kristen Hadley, Alvin Huang, Avery C. Hunker, Atlas Jordan, Zoe C. Juneau, Matthew Jungert, Madhav Kannan, Inkar Kapen, Shannon Khem, Megan Koch, Katalin Kocsis, Rana Kutsal, Gabriela León, Matt Mallory, Jocelin Malone, Audrey McCutcheon, Medea McGraw, Kamiliam Nasirova, Dakota Newman, Lindsay Ng, Ximena Opitz-Araya, Alana Oyama, Elliot Phillips, Christina Alice Pom, Lydia Potekhina, Ramkumar Rajanbabu, Shea T. Ransford, Ingrid Redford, Christine Rimorin, Dana Rocha, Augustin Ruiz, Naz Taskin, Michael Tieu, Éva Tóth, Jessica Trinh, Marshall VanNess, Sara Vargas, Maria Camila Vergara, Morgan Wirthlin, Jeanelle Ariza, Trygve Bakken, Nick Dee, Nikolai D